---
// The six print() lines from the p10_print capture, with the honest answer to
// "which request printed this?". Lines 1-2 cannot be told apart even by
// reading the code; 3-6 are known only from the sleep times in the demo and
// the order of the two uvicorn access lines in the capture.
const W = 900, H = 300;
const rows = [
  { en: 'closing case', vi: 'closing case', who: '?', red: true },
  { en: 'closing case', vi: 'closing case', who: '?', red: true },
  { en: 'rule check passed', vi: 'rule check passed', who: 'C-2', red: false },
  { en: 'done', vi: 'done', who: 'C-2', red: false },
  { en: 'rule check passed', vi: 'rule check passed', who: 'C-1', red: false },
  { en: 'done', vi: 'done', who: 'C-1', red: false },
];
---
<figure class="bep10a">
  <div class="bep10a-scroll">
  <svg viewBox={`0 0 ${W} ${H}`} role="img" aria-label="Six print lines from two overlapping requests. The first two lines both read closing case and the figure marks them with a question mark in red, because nothing says which request printed them. The other four are attributed to C-2 twice and C-1 twice, but only by reading the code.">
    <text x="40" y="30" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>what print() left behind</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>print() để lại gì</tspan></text>
    <text x="520" y="30" class="h"><tspan data-lang-en>which request printed it?</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>request nào in ra?</tspan></text>
    <line x1="40" y1="42" x2="860" y2="42" class="axis" />
    {rows.map((r, i) => (
      <g>
        <text x="40" y={72 + i * 34} class="ln"><tspan data-lang-en>{i + 1}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{i + 1}</tspan></text>
        <text x="80" y={72 + i * 34} class="msg"><tspan data-lang-en>{r.en}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{r.vi}</tspan></text>
        <text x="520" y={72 + i * 34} class={r.red ? 'who red' : 'who'}><tspan data-lang-en>{r.who}</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>{r.who}</tspan></text>
      </g>
    ))}
    <text x="620" y="106" class="note"><tspan data-lang-en>not even the code can say</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>đọc code cũng không biết</tspan></text>
    <text x="620" y="208" class="note"><tspan data-lang-en>guessable only from sleep times</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>chỉ đoán được từ thời gian sleep</tspan></text>
    <text x="620" y="236" class="note"><tspan data-lang-en>and the access-log order</tspan><tspan data-lang-vi>và thứ tự dòng access log</tspan></text>
  </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption>
    <span data-lang-en>The six lines are the real capture above. Two requests overlapped and one stream swallowed the difference: a log line needs the request it belongs to written on it.</span>
    <span data-lang-vi>Sáu dòng này lấy đúng từ capture phía trên. Hai request chạy chồng nhau và một luồng output nuốt mất ranh giới: mỗi dòng log phải mang theo request mà nó thuộc về.</span>
  </figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
  .bep10a { margin: 2em 0; width: 100%; }
  .bep10a-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .bep10a svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; }
  .bep10a text { font-size: 14px; fill: var(--text-body); font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .bep10a .h { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); font-size: 15px; }
  .bep10a .ln { fill: var(--text-faint); }
  .bep10a .who { font-weight: 700; fill: var(--text); }
  .bep10a .who.red { fill: var(--red); }
  .bep10a .note { fill: var(--text-muted); font-size: 13px; }
  .bep10a .axis { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.4; }
  .bep10a figcaption { margin-top: 10px; font-size: 14px; color: var(--text-muted); line-height: 1.55; text-align: center; }
</style>
